[Music]  good spin-offs require delicate  balancing acts lean too heavily in one  direction and you stray from the source  material lean too far in the other and  you're little more than fanservice  a good spin-off takes advantage of the  world that's sprang from without being  beholden to it this is no easy task  maybe that's why the very words spin off  is often used as a pejorative  with so many offshoots of movie  franchises and television shows many  tend to fall by the cultural wayside  they're forgettable and pandering  excuses to waste time until the next  full season or blockbuster sequel arrive  but of course spin-offs can also be a  thing of beauty as long as there has  been entertainment there have been  supporting characters that draw so much  attention they break into their own  starring roles from Cheers came Frasier  from Breaking Bad came better call Saul  from Shrek came Puss in Boots nothing  will distract me  Oh video games are no strangers to the  phenomenon in fact some modern  franchises are built on their spin-off  potential some became so successful in  ubiquitous on their own you might be  surprised to learn that they even began  as spin-offs and while it hasn't  eclipsed the scope and quality of its  original source material the recent  throne breaker The Witcher tales has  earned a spot among the pantheon of  great spin-off video games  it carries CD Projekt RED or say they  project Reds world into a new genre it  tells a story from a different  perspective and it sets itself apart  from the universe that spawned it and in  doing so it has become the perfect video  game spin-off  if you played The Witcher 3 you've  probably tried your hand at Gwent the  in-universe collectible card game is  played across the northern kingdoms  pitting travelers against each other in  homes and taverns alike throne breaker  on the other hand rips Gwent from the  confines of the witcher 3 and places it  at the center of an entirely new RPG you  fill the shoes of Queen Eve ruler of  Rivia and leiria during the second  nilfgaardian invasion basically it's a  prequel to the first Witcher game it's a  reward of its own to explore the places  and meet the characters we've only heard  about in the original trilogy but throne  breaker takes things further using memes  unique perspective as Queen to tell a  story about the burden of leadership and  the difficult choices she has to make  these dilemmas are essential part of  throne breakers story between battles  the RPG places you in Sophie's Choice  scenarios that avoid the usual black and  white of simpler games  sergeant oh man a 15 summers amol will  join our ranks at once they'll serve 5  years I think perspective is a key  factor in any good spinoff better call  Saul recognized the humor and  storytelling potential in Bob Odenkirk  character and used his occupations as a  con man and a lawyer to show another  side of the justice system in the  American Southwest The Witcher 3 to use  the most recent series entry is about a  lone wanderer in a dangerous world  throne breaker shows us that same world  from a different social stratum 1 in  which Trust plays a much larger role as  Neves allegiance as sought from numerous  angles after all few people ever bowed  to Geralt of Rivia the shift and  storytelling perspective is aided of  course by a shift in gameplay as opposed  to the third-person action of its RPG  predecessors throne breaker uses the  strategy and collecting of a card game  to drive its action this fits well in a  game where you play as a leader you  travel the kingdoms recruiting new  soldiers or cards to your cause you  bolster Army's might as you fight  nilfgaard across a variety of locales  throne breaker does have problems with  difficulty spikes or in some cases a  complete lack of difficulty but more  often the rules of Gwent make for  challenging and rewarding battles throne  breaker is at its very best when it  embraces the puzzle aspects  of certain scenarios take this fight for  instance against an al Ghul in The  Witcher 3 these enemies can regenerate  their own health  forcing Geralt to stay on the offensive  in throne breaker that ability is much  more dangerous by consuming dead units  from the enemy deck the al Ghul absorbs  their health becoming stronger with each  passing turn and making the fight more  difficult the longer you take so in both  cases al Ghul's are dangerous but in  throne breaker there's a new twist on  that danger it's a microcosm for the  spinoff as a whole it takes aspects of  the universe we're familiar with and  asks us to see them through a new lens  it's important to note at this point  that I don't normally gravitate toward  collectible card games I dabbled in  hearthstone when it first released but  by and large the genre just doesn't grab  me I've always preferred the flexibility  of a turn-based tactics game to the more  rigid rules of a CCG but throne breaker  grabs me and it didn't let go I came for  The Witcher world but I stayed for the  characters and more surprisingly the  nuanced card combat it's based in a  universe I adore but it's eased me into  a genre I don't normally care for by  offering new perspectives both in terms  of story and overall genre throne  breaker pulled me out of my comfort zone  and I could not be happier about it as I  mentioned already there are numerous  flaws and throne breaker its difficulty  is all over the place its story slows to  a crawl in too many spots  it also overstays its welcome by 5 hours  or so as with every other video game  thrown breaker is not perfect but in its  function as a spin-off throne breaker is  perfect it adds to the witcher world  without retreading it it makes great use  of source material without being  hindered by it there's much more than  fanservice here but fans will find  plenty to love now that I've beaten  throne breaker I can't wait to see where  else CD Projekt can take the witcher  universe if this one is any indication  future witcher spin-offs will demand my  attention  you

